{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The four rules"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Pure value patch → computed property"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"type":"text","text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Flag, don’t fake","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"na